Z||000002||theogre||05-12-2000||06:40 PM||||I have to doubt the effectiveness of this as a power enhancement. Also it would only work in a very narrow range of temperatures. Below the range the effect would disappear quickly. Above the range it could cause some annoying, even nasty problems.<P>Both the MAT and Coolant temp sensors have the same resistance curves. The resistance is in the thousands of Ohms at lower temp but drops to a near short at higher temp. As the temp rises above your induced error's effective range it's posible to set codes in the ECM.||||reg||1
